+---
+id: dl-003-long-rental-discount-rounds-to-the-nearest-cent-applies-to-the-whole-rental-from-3-days
+type: decision-log
+title: "Long-rental discount rounds to the nearest cent, applies to the whole rental from 3 days"
+status: pending
+---
+
+<!-- decision-log body. `wingfoil memory add` copies this scaffold verbatim; `memory submit` replaces
+     these placeholder comments with real content and fills the required frontmatter fields. -->
+
+## Context
+
+Customers staying 3 days or more get 10% off. Totals are integer euro cents, so the discount can leave a fraction of a cent.
+
+## Decision
+
+The 10% applies to the whole rental, not only to days beyond the third. The reduced total is computed in
+integer arithmetic (`full * 90 / 100`) and rounded to the nearest cent with `Math.round`, which is
+deterministic. `quote` carries the rule and `book` reuses it, so both always show the same total.
+
+## Consequences
+
+Total stays an integer number of cents. The price jumps down in per-day terms at 3 days (a 3-day rental
+is never cheaper than a 2-day one in total, but its per-day price is 10% lower), which is the intended reward
+for longer stays.
